                        "sense_id": "3f06451c-51e4-3574-a291-a586ab3eb1d0",
                        "entry_id": "2932e27c-70da-37c1-aa86-31240fb0d002",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stimulating the vagus nerve."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0b3488f-aa47-4b3a-be2a-3857c0274b62",
                                "sense_id": "3f06451c-51e4-3574-a291-a586ab3eb1d0",
                                "text": "Capelle and Bayer believe that both the thyroid gland and the thymus gland produce an internal secretion that has two components, one sympathicotropic and one vagotropic."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "01cae76b-621c-4f3a-876a-0b92228e82ce",
                                "sense_id": "3f06451c-51e4-3574-a291-a586ab3eb1d0",
                                "text": "These “vagotropic” actions can be referred to decreased irritability of the sympathetic nerve-endings."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "300915ea-317f-4c2f-8ab4-ef143ab1ac40",
                                "sense_id": "3f06451c-51e4-3574-a291-a586ab3eb1d0",
                                "text": "This corresponds, as the authors stress, with our law since the epileptics are, after attacks, in a vagotonic situation; they therefore respond less to vagotropic stimuli."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
